{
 "result": "csvsum.py is a working body. It reads sys.stdin.buffer, splits lines, skips the header, parses each val with float, groups values per cat, sums each group with math.fsum, and writes sorted 'cat,sum' lines formatted with %.2f. It matches the public sample out-0.txt. Its registered baseline is 1.883 with 4.4% noise. The one variant tried (single split(b',', 2) unpack, bound dict getter) scored 1.912 against 1.895 for the incumbent, which is inside noise, so it was not adopted. I am resting rather than spending the remaining 38 energy on another attempt, because the obvious remaining speedups either change the summation (plain sum instead of fsum, risking last-digit differences at 2 decimals) or are within measurement noise.",
